Now in candidate, targetClass lines are removed. Need to locate the code removal locations. Find lines 28 and 42 in previous. Provide candidate_location referencing where removal occurs? The spec: candidate_location refers to location in candidate where change is reflected (i.e., absence?). For removal, candidate_location maybe points to location after removal? Could be same line numbers where removal would be inserted? But we can provide location of removal anchor using previous location maybe but candidate location could be where removal is manifested (perhaps start at line after removal?). Might be tricky, but we can give previous_location for each removal and candidate_location maybe same start/end as previous? Might be acceptable.

